330	## Web Security
331	
332	### XSS Prevention
333	
334	```perl
335	use v5.36;
336	use HTML::Entities qw(encode_entities);
337	use URI::Escape qw(uri_escape_utf8);
338	
339	# Good: Encode output for HTML context
340	sub safe_html($user_input) {
341	    return encode_entities($user_input);
342	}
343	
344	# Good: Encode for URL context
345	sub safe_url_param($value) {
346	    return uri_escape_utf8($value);
347	}
348	
349	# Good: Encode for JSON context
350	use JSON::MaybeXS qw(encode_json);
351	sub safe_json($data) {
352	    return encode_json($data);  # Handles escaping
353	}
354	
355	# Template auto-escaping (Mojolicious)
356	# <%= $user_input %>   — auto-escaped (safe)
357	# <%== $raw_html %>    — raw output (dangerous, use only for trusted content)
358	
359	# Template auto-escaping (Template Toolkit)
360	# [% user_input | html %]  — explicit HTML encoding
361	
362	# Bad: Raw output in HTML
363	sub bad_html($input) {
364	    print "<div>$input</div>";  # XSS if $input contains <script>
365	}
366	```
367	
368	### CSRF Protection
369	
370	```perl
371	use v5.36;
372	use Crypt::URandom qw(urandom);
373	use MIME::Base64 qw(encode_base64url);
374	
375	sub generate_csrf_token() {
376	    return encode_base64url(urandom(32));
377	}
378	```
379	
380	Use constant-time comparison when verifying tokens. Most web frameworks (Mojolicious, Dancer2, Catalyst) provide built-in CSRF protection — prefer those over hand-rolled solutions.
381	
382	### Session and Header Security
383	
384	```perl
385	use v5.36;
386	
387	# Mojolicious session + headers
388	$app->secrets(['long-random-secret-rotated-regularly']);
389	$app->sessions->secure(1);          # HTTPS only
390	$app->sessions->samesite('Lax');
391	
392	$app->hook(after_dispatch => sub ($c) {
393	    $c->res->headers->header('X-Content-Type-Options' => 'nosniff');
394	    $c->res->headers->header('X-Frame-Options'        => 'DENY');
395	    $c->res->headers->header('Content-Security-Policy' => "default-src 'self'");
396	    $c->res->headers->header('Strict-Transport-Security' => 'max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains');
397	});
398	```
399	
400	## Output Encoding
401	
402	Always encode output for its context: `HTML::Entities::encode_entities()` for HTML, `URI::Escape::uri_escape_utf8()` for URLs, `JSON::MaybeXS::encode_json()` for JSON.
403	
404	## CPAN Module Security
405	
406	- **Pin versions** in cpanfile: `requires 'DBI', '== 1.643';`
407	- **Prefer maintained modules**: Check MetaCPAN for recent releases
408	- **Minimize dependencies**: Each dependency is an attack surface
409	
410	## Security Tooling
411	
412	### perlcritic Security Policies
413	
414	```ini
415	# .perlcriticrc — security-focused configuration
416	severity = 3
417	theme = security + core
418	
419	# Require three-arg open
420	[InputOutput::RequireThreeArgOpen]
421	severity = 5
422	
423	# Require checked system calls
424	[InputOutput::RequireCheckedSyscalls]
425	functions = :builtins
426	severity = 4
427	
428	# Prohibit string eval
429	[BuiltinFunctions::ProhibitStringyEval]
430	severity = 5
431	
432	# Prohibit backtick operators
433	[InputOutput::ProhibitBacktickOperators]
434	severity = 4
435	
436	# Require taint checking in CGI
437	[Modules::RequireTaintChecking]
438	severity = 5
439	
440	# Prohibit two-arg open
441	[InputOutput::ProhibitTwoArgOpen]
442	severity = 5
443	
444	# Prohibit bare-word filehandles
445	[InputOutput::ProhibitBarewordFileHandles]
446	severity = 5
447	```
448	
449	### Running perlcritic
450	
451	```bash
452	# Check a file
453	perlcritic --severity 3 --theme security lib/MyApp/Handler.pm
454	
455	# Check entire project
456	perlcritic --severity 3 --theme security lib/
457	
458	# CI integration
459	perlcritic --severity 4 --theme security --quiet lib/ || exit 1
460	```
461	
462	## Quick Security Checklist
463	
464	| Check | What to Verify |
465	|---|---|
466	| Taint mode | `-T` flag on CGI/web scripts |
467	| Input validation | Allowlist patterns, length limits |
468	| File operations | Three-arg open, path traversal checks |
469	| Process execution | List-form system, no shell interpolation |
470	| SQL queries | DBI placeholders, never interpolate |
471	| HTML output | `encode_entities()`, template auto-escape |
472	| CSRF tokens | Generated, verified on state-changing requests |
473	| Session config | Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookies |
474	| HTTP headers | CSP, X-Frame-Options, HSTS |
475	| Dependencies | Pinned versions, audited modules |
476	| Regex safety | No nested quantifiers, anchored patterns |
477	| Error messages | No stack traces or paths leaked to users |
478	
479	## Anti-Patterns
480	
481	```perl
482	# 1. Two-arg open with user data (command injection)
483	open my $fh, $user_input;               # CRITICAL vulnerability
484	
485	# 2. String-form system (shell injection)
486	system("convert $user_file output.png"); # CRITICAL vulnerability
487	
488	# 3. SQL string interpolation
489	$dbh->do("DELETE FROM users WHERE id = $id");  # SQLi
490	
491	# 4. eval with user input (code injection)
492	eval $user_code;                         # Remote code execution
493	
494	# 5. Trusting $ENV without sanitizing
495	my $path = $ENV{UPLOAD_DIR};             # Could be manipulated
496	system("ls $path");                      # Double vulnerability
497	
498	# 6. Disabling taint without validation
499	($input) = $input =~ /(.*)/s;           # Lazy untaint — defeats purpose
